 prf-story\">As of Oct 12, Perry County&rsquo;s record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, and November to December came in under 90% of normal in 37 of them. In 2025, August to September ran 23% of normal on the middle of the grids, and September to October ran 40%. Grid 14870 had its driest year in 1954 at 54%. For 2026 so far, May to June stands at 182% on the middle of the grids, while February to March sat at 46%.</p>"}
